2026-10-10T23:42:18.2815505Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2901493Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2910326Z [0m
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2910866Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2911307Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2911496Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2912047Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2912670Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2912990Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2913281Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2913738Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2913945Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2914988Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2915644Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2916010Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2916492Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2916619Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2916803Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2917005Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2917208Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2917503Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2917603Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2917709Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2917837Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2918143Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2918532Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2921500Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2921604Z I will:
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2921703Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2921864Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2922205Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2922738Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2923228Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2923518Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2923759Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2924323Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2924899Z    /root
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2934618Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2935272Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2944865Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2945500Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2945956Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2946498Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2947091Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2962292Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2963022Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2972212Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2972704Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2973268Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2973500Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2973701Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2973964Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2974295Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-10T23:42:18.2974950Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
